format 1
adapter statements 1
unit: inside-the-atom

statement inside-the-atom-s01
verdict: fact
statement: Everything you can touch, and the air around you, is made of atoms.

explanation:
    Solids, liquids and gases are all made of atoms. Even air is.

statement inside-the-atom-s02
verdict: myth
statement: Light and heat are made of atoms, just like a rock is.

explanation:
    Light and heat are not matter. They are not made of atoms.

statement inside-the-atom-s03
verdict: fact
statement: Every atom has a tiny centre called the nucleus, with electrons around it.

explanation:
    The nucleus sits in the middle and the electrons are around it.

statement inside-the-atom-s04
verdict: myth
statement: Neutrons have a negative charge.

explanation:
    Neutrons have no charge. Electrons are the negative ones.

statement inside-the-atom-s05
verdict: fact
statement: Protons are positive, electrons are negative, and neutrons have no charge.

explanation:
    These three charges are what each particle of an atom is like.

statement inside-the-atom-s06
verdict: myth
statement: If an atom gains a neutron, it becomes a different element.

explanation:
    The number of protons decides the element. A different number of neutrons only makes a different isotope.

statement inside-the-atom-s07
verdict: fact
statement: The number of protons in an atom tells you which element it is.

explanation:
    Every carbon atom has 6 protons and every oxygen atom has 8.

statement inside-the-atom-s08
verdict: myth
statement: An isotope is always radioactive.

explanation:
    Many isotopes are perfectly stable. An isotope is not automatically radioactive.

statement inside-the-atom-s09
verdict: fact
statement: Isotopes of one element have the same number of protons but different numbers of neutrons.

explanation:
    Same protons means same element. Different neutrons means a different isotope.

statement inside-the-atom-s10
verdict: myth
statement: Every nucleus is unstable and will change one day.

explanation:
    Some nuclei stay the same for ever. Only unstable ones can change.
